Global Affairs Canada's per-country feed (https://data.international.gc.ca/travel-voyage/cta-cap-<iso>.json)
for the 13 guides with avoid-zone marks (scripts/stay-skip.json "marks"), fetched 2026-10-30 01:35 EDT and
trimmed to data.country-iso, data.advisory-state and data.eng's name, url-slug and advisories (what
fxtracker/watchouts.py reads for the regional blocks; the trimmed copy parses to the same blocks as the whole
page). The day the marks' words were checked: scripts/test_avoid_marks.py finds the words of every mark
checked on 2026-10-30 (FIXDAY in the test), verbatim and in order, in the block whose fingerprint the mark
carries.
Re-checking a mark (DEPLOY.md, "Re-check a row") leaves these files alone: its later "checked" date takes it
off them, the test holds it to the table only, and gen_stay_spots.py --check verifies its words on the live
feed. Never edit or refetch one file here (the other marks of that day are held to it). To move the offline
proof to a later day: fetch every marked country into a new gac-<date> folder, re-check every mark against
it, and point FIXDIR and FIXDAY in the test at it.
